WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.390
Hank: I think they can see us a little bit.

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.350
John: I don't think they can see us.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.479
H: They're thirsty for Augustus Waters, John.

00:00:04.479 --> 00:00:05.499
J: Is that what it said?

00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:05.979
H: Yeah.

00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:10.730
J: Haha, that's a funny pun, 'cause he's Waters.
It's an import- it's an important metaphor

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:11.030
in the book.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.440
J: Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday ... It's
actually Monday, we're on our way to The Fault

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.490
In Our Stars move premiere. It's very exciting.
The collaboration between the two of us and

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.390
the community that's emerged from it means
more to me than anything else in my professional

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.519
life, and before we go do this crazy thing,
I just wanna say thank you.

00:00:26.519 --> 00:00:29.199
Hank: You're welcome. Also thank you.

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:31.710
J: That's what I was waiting for, the mutual
thank-you!

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.670
(Crowd screaming)

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:41.670
J: Hold on, I 
have to video-blog really quickly. Instead
of a red carpet, we have a TFIOS blue carpet,

00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:51.730
how awesome is that?

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:52.399
J (voiceover): So Hank, we signed for some
people who'd lined up to go to see the premiere,

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:54.309
and then said hi to a lot more people who
had Okay cloud posters by which time my brain

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:54.370
was slightly fried.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:59.010
J: Okay Hank, I have successfully signed a
bunch of uh... posters and everything not

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:03.010
skin. That's my rule, anything that's not
skin and I am back on the magic TFIOS blue

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:03.629
carpet.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:08.590
So Hank currently across from me are like
a large wall of photographers, uh that's,

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:12.160
hence all the flashes, but I need to tell
you that The Fault in Our Stars movie is coming

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:18.340
out on Friday. This Friday. Like the day after
the day after tomorrow. Unless you go to The

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.150
Night Before Our Stars, in which case it's
coming out the day after tomorrow.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.260
If you want to see it on Thursday, at least
in some cities that is still possible, you

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:27.420
can go to thefaultinourstarsmovie.com and
get tickets, link in the doobly doo.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.690
I am sweating through my Burberry shirt, which
is only increasing my already sizable anxiety.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:32.950
J: Aww, you look so cute!

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.960
J (voiceover): Then Nat Wolff showed up for
our Today Show live chat.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.730
J: There are people from The Today Show talking
to me inside of my ear.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.250
J (voiceover): And then came the live chat
with our astonishingly beautiful and talented

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:41.930
Hazel, Shailene Woodley.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:46.340
By the time that was over, things were starting
to get quite crowed. I met Indy 500 winner

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:47.450
Ryan Hunter-Reay.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.870
Then things got even more crowed and I kind
of lost my ability to even.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:56.300
J: I don't know, I don't know what to say,
I don't have, I don't have a... I don't have

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.540
J (voiceover): Took a selfie with Mike Birbiglia,
and then stood on the carpet with my brilliant

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:02.800
and lovely wife just a few feet away from
Shailene and Laura Dern.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:08.539
And then, I got to meet Spelling Bee co-champion
Ansun Sujoe, unquestionably the highlight

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:09.570
of my evening!

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:12.910
Okay Hank, I just did all of those press interviews
and now I am going to into the movie, look!

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.530
Look look look look look! That's the movie!

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.140
Well Hank, they didn't let me film inside
the theatre, so greetings from Tuesday, where

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.410
my view of Manhattan is not half bad.
Hank, the premiere was just absolutely amazing

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:27.420
- laughing and crying with 1200 people, and
I'm so glad that you were sitting there, two

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.670
seats away from me.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:31.790
So Hank, before I say anything else, I just
wanna establish that I'm not getting paid

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:35.610
for the movie, like I got paid for the rights
a long time ago, but I don't get a percentage

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:40.380
of ticket sales or anything, and I don't have
to talk about it. And if I didn't like it,

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.790
believe me, you'd know.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:46.440
But in fact, I love the movie; I think it's
amazingly faithful to the book, and powerful,

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.260
and funny, and moving.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:51.110
Hank, the people who made this movie cared
about the story, and they care about each

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:53.150
other, and you can really see that.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:56.610
Last night we all got to be together one last
time, which was sad in a way but it was also

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.600
very exciting, because it means that soon,
in fact very soon, EVERYONE will get to see

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.180
the movie.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.770
Thanks to all of Nerdfighteria for being part
of this process with me - read the book first!

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:09.690
And Hank, I will see you on Friday - when
The Fault In Our Stars movie will be out in

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:10.930
theatres everywhere!

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:17.930
Nat: 'How you doing, Hank? Well, so I kind
of, y'know it was a great premiere that we

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.910
had, but, y'know, okay, Hank.'

